I think I found a small bug in Denys Duchier's tab.sty. In the following
macro definition

\def\@tabarg[#1]{%
  \@tempdima#1\relax
  \ifdim\@tempdima>\z@
    \unskip
    \advance\@tempdima \dp\@arstrut
    \vrule\@depth\@tempdima\@width\z@
  \else
    \gdef\@tabup{\vskip\@tempdima}\fi
  \@tabeolpeek}

I had to replace
    \advance\@tempdima \dp\@arstrut
with
    \advance\@tempdima \dp\@arstrutbox
to make
    \\[0.5pc]
inside a `tabular' work. \@arstrut is just a macro that does a =
\(unh)copy
of \@arstrutbox.

Nico

